82,"_83":84},{"_56":66,"_58":67,"_60":68,"_69":70},{"_56":57,"_58":59,"_60":61,"_62":63},"type","links","field","originalImage","label","Original creator image","items",[64],{"_60":61,"_27":65},"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0045cc0c-b7c0-4c99-be13-c13f2c66cef2","text","mediaReviewed","Screenshot source reviewed","value","2026-10-20","image","gameplay","The creator’s in-game title screen and supermarket scene; this is not a GameMap execution of the Windows release.","src","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/supermarket-simulator-cursor.webp","alt","The creator’s running supermarket game at its title menu, showing store shelves and two characters.","https://github.com/breineng/supermarket-simulator#description","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","Creator-published screenshot","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)",[89],"Cursor","Related resources",[94],"resourceIds","section",{"_60":95,"_27":96},"Unity · Manual","/resources/unity-engine/","Creator evidence",[100],"evidence",{"_60":101,"_27":78,"_102":103},"Read the creator’s AI attribution","note","Author README names coding models, Hunyuan assets, source setup and a linked creation video. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[108],{"_60":109,"_27":110,"_102":111},"Open the complete game project","https://github.com/breineng/supermarket-simulator","Complete Unity 2023.2.6f1 project with Assets, Packages and ProjectSettings. Scenes, prefabs and models use Git LFS: clone with LFS and run git lfs pull before opening Assets/Scenes/InitScene.unity. MIT code; Unity, generated models and dependencies retain their terms. LFS objects were not fetched in this review.","Access type","download","demo","Play or run",[117],{"_60":118,"_27":119,"_102":120},"Download the Windows game","https://github.com/breineng/supermarket-simulator/releases/download/0.0.1/SupermarketSimulator.zip","Windows download, about 397 MB, from release 0.0.1. Extract and run Supermaket Simulator.exe. Other platforms require a source build; the binary was not downloaded or executed in this review.","Game platform","GitHub Releases","Guide format","disclosure","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[128],{"_60":129,"_27":78,"_102":-7},"Read the creator’s development disclosure","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[134,135,136,137],"Download the Windows release and try the order, delivery, stocking and checkout loop.","Read the creator’s build account and linked video to separate coding assistance from generated models.","Clone with Git LFS, fetch the LFS objects and open InitScene in the matching Unity editor.","Adjust one stock, customer or checkout behavior with an agent, then compare a complete customer-service loop.","AI workflow / foundation context","The author names Cursor with Gemini 2.5 Pro, Claude Opus 4 and Claude Sonnet 4, and links a creation video. The fully AI-generated description is a creator claim; the public source separates the Unity project and Hunyuan model work.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","3D","track","metadata","Engine","Unity 2023.2.6f1 · URP · C#","engine","lead","3d","ai-assisted",[134,135,136,137],{"_60":129,"_27":78,"_19":124},{"_60":118,"_27":119,"_19":113,"_102":120},{"_60":109,"_27":110,"_102":111,"_163":164},{"_60":101,"_27":78,"_102":103},[162],"unity-engine","scope","complete-project","example:morbreaker-unity-claude","morbreaker-unity-claude","morBreaker","Clear ten brick-breaker levels with a paddle-controlled ball that accelerates on bounces, rising brick durability, and locally saved high scores.","/examples/morbreaker-unity-claude/",{"_21":166,"_23":167,"_25":168,"_152":228,"_148":229,"_144":155,"_140":226,"_9":230,"_125":231,"_114":232,"_34":233,"_99":234,"_92":235},[172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190],{"_56":23,"_69":167,"_58":23,"_93":-7},{"_56":153,"_69":168,"_58":25,"_93":-7},{"_56":66,"_60":150,"_69":228,"_58":152,"_93":141},{"_56":66,"_60":146,"_69":227,"_58":148,"_93":149},{"_56":66,"_60":142,"_69":143,"_58":144,"_93":145},{"_56":66,"_60":138,"_69":226,"_58":140,"_93":141},{"_56":85,"_60":130,"_131":132,"_62":221,"_58":9,"_93":-7},{"_56":57,"_60":126,"_62":218,"_58":125,"_93":-7},{"_56":66,"_60":123,"_69":124,"_58":125,"_93":-7},{"_56":66,"_60":121,"_69":122,"_58":114,"_93":-7},{"_56":57,"_60":115,"_62":213,"_58":114,"_93":-7},{"_56":66,"_60":112,"_69":113,"_58":114,"_93":-7},{"_56":57,"_60":106,"_62":209,"_58":34,"_93":-7},{"_56":66,"_60":104,"_69":105,"_58":34,"_93":-7},{"_56":57,"_60":97,"_62":204,"_58":99,"_93":-7},{"_56":57,"_60":90,"_62":200,"_58":92,"_93":-7},{"_56":85,"_58":86,"_60":87,"_62":198},{"_56":71,"_58":72,"_60":193,"_74":194,"_76":195,"_34":196,"_79":80,"_81":82,"_83":197},{"_56":66,"_58":191,"_60":192,"_69":70},"captureDate","Screenshot captured","Gameplay captured from the creator’s published WebGL build.","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/morbreaker-unity-claude.webp","morBreaker gameplay with a paddle, ball, coloured brick grid, and score display.","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker","GameMap local capture",[199],"Claude Code",[201,202],{"_60":95,"_27":96},{"_60":199,"_27":203},"/resources/claude-code/",[205],{"_60":206,"_27":207,"_102":208},"Read the explicit Claude Code contribution breakdown","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker#built-with-claude-code-","Creator disclosure names the Unity MCP package and lists the editor work Claude performed. It is a process summary, not a published prompt transcript.",[210],{"_60":211,"_27":196,"_102":212},"Open the complete Unity game","MIT-licensed Assets, Packages, ProjectSettings, scenes, and C# gameplay source. Requires Unity 6000.4.11f1; open Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity and press Play. Windows/WebGL build modules are needed only for packaging; Claude/MCP tooling is not required for play.",[214],{"_60":215,"_27":216,"_102":217},"Download morBreaker for Windows or WebGL","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker/releases/tag/v1.2.0","Version 1.2.0 includes Windows standalone and WebGL ZIPs. Extract the Windows build and launch it, or serve the WebGL build over HTTP. A/D or arrows move, Space launches, H shows scores, and Space/Enter restarts. Pointer/touch controls are included; no public hosted play link is supplied.",[219],{"_60":220,"_27":207,"_102":-7},"Read the creator’s Unity and Claude Code account",[222,223,224,225],"Download the Windows release or serve the published WebGL build over HTTP.","Try paddle steering, acceleration, loss, restart, and the local score list.","Read the creator’s Claude Code disclosure and inspect the gameplay C# scripts.","Open SampleScene.unity with Unity 6000.4.11f1, change one level rule, and test progression.","KingMordas says Claude Code built almost the entire game through the Unity MCP plugin: gameplay scripts, scene and prefab wiring, tests, and documentation. The AI editor tooling is separate from the released game runtime.","2D","Unity 6 · URP · C#","2d",[222,223,224,225],{"_60":220,"_27":207,"_19":124},{"_60":215,"_27":216,"_19":113,"_102":217},{"_60":211,"_27":196,"_163":164,"_102":212},{"_60":206,"_27":207,"_102":208},[162,236],"claude-code","resource:unity-engine","resource","Official Unity documentation for projects, the editor, scripting, rendering, physics, asset import, and publishing.","/resources/",{"_21":162,"_304":95,"_144":305,"_56":306,"_303":239,"_298":297,"_27":295,"_57":307,"_284":308,"_275":309,"_272":310,"_268":267},[244,245,246,247,248,249,250,251,252,253,254,255,256],"website/src/data/resources.json",{"_56":23,"_69":95,"_58":304,"_93":-7},{"_56":153,"_69":239,"_58":303,"_93":-7},{"_56":66,"_60":301,"_69":302,"_58":144,"_93":149},{"_56":66,"_60":299,"_69":300,"_58":56,"_93":149},{"_56":66,"_60":296,"_69":297,"_58":298,"_93":141},{"_56":57,"_60":106,"_62":293,"_58":27,"_93":-7},{"_56":57,"_60":289,"_62":29